-- title:
--   Translation on the twisted commutant scales Haar by ‖det t‖_L⁻¹
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ a finite Galois extension with $[L:K]=2$, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by the integral powers of $\sigma$. Fix $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, a unit $c$ of $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$ and an idele $u \in \mathbb{A}_K^\times$, and put $\delta = (\delta_0 \otimes 1)\cdot c\,I_2 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$, where $\delta_0$ is pushed forward along $L \to L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$, $x \mapsto x \otimes 1$. Assume the hypothesis `hN`, which says that the product $\prod_{i=0}^{[L:K]-1}\sigma^i(\delta) = \delta\,\sigma(\delta)$, with $\sigma$ acting on $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$ through the left factor and entrywise on matrices, equals the scalar matrix with diagonal entry $1 \otimes u$. Let $R$ be the twisted commutant, i.e. the $K$-subalgebra $\{X \in M_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K) : X\delta = \delta\,\sigma(X)\}$, equipped with any measurable space structure that is its Borel structure, and let $\alpha$ be an additive Haar measure on $R$. Let $t$ lie in the twisted centralizer $\{t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K) : t\,\delta\,\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$, which the project's multiplicative equivalence [`AutomorphicForm.twistedCentralizerEquivUnits`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedCommutant.html#L98) identifies with the unit group $R^\times$. Then the push-forward of $\alpha$ under left multiplication $x \mapsto tx$ on $R$, and likewise the push-forward under right multiplication $x \mapsto xt$, both equal $\|\det t\|^{-1}\cdot\alpha$, where $\|\cdot\|$ is `distribHaarChar` of $\mathbb{A}_L$ and $\det t$ is read in $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ through the composite ring isomorphism $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \cong \mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ given by `Algebra.TensorProduct.comm` followed by [`M4aHerbrand.Bridge.genuineRingEquiv`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineTensorEquiv.html#L57).
--
--   This is the adelic module computation for the twisted commutant of a $\sigma$-conjugacy class with central norm: when $\delta_0$ is $\sigma$-conjugate to no scalar, $R$ is the ring of adelic points of a quaternion algebra over $K$ and the statement is the classical formula for the module of its idele group acting on its adele ring by translations. It is used to convert a condition on the idelic module of the determinant into measure preservation, in the construction of a compact set absorbing twisted centralizer elements of module one.
